          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a note says \"use additional code\", is that optional?",
          "answer": "The passages I retrieved do not say whether \"use additional code\" is optional or mandatory, so I can't give you a firm answer from them.\n\nWhat they do say about the note type:\n\n- **\"Code first\" and \"use additional code\" work as a pair.** They set the order of reporting. The underlying condition is reported first, and its manifestation is added after it. (Source: *ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection*)\n- **\"Code also\" means two codes are needed,** but it does not set which comes first. (Same source)\n- **In practice, the additional code adds detail.** For example, diabetic chronic kidney disease is paired with a code for the stage of kidney disease. (Source: *Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories*)\n\nFor the optional-or-mandatory question, the official ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting are the authoritative place to check. A certified medical coder or the clinician who wrote the record can also tell you how the note applies in a specific case.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
